"""Training-context alignment ablation for the controlled Gold benchmark.

Probe-local scoring recovered memorisation while raw generic aggregation and a
content-difficulty residual did not.  One remaining confounder is context
construction: probe-local scoring recreated the exact positive-control training
suffix (BOS + up to 254 payload bytes + EOS), whereas the generic Stage2 scorer
uses ordinary content windows without that training wrapper.

This module isolates that difference.  It knows only that the frozen positive-
control training window was the suffix; it never receives the probe text or
boundary.  It scores *all* payload bytes in the training-aligned suffix and
compares a small frozen set of generic summaries with the same-run raw Stage2
Loss baseline.  Labels are joined only after both architecture feature tables
are sealed.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import json
import math
from pathlib import Path
from typing import Any, Mapping, Sequence

import numpy as np
import pandas as pd

from . import shadow_gold_kaggle as gold_v1
from . import shadow_gold_kaggle_v2 as gold_v2
